The Vaccine Adverse Event Reporting System (VAERS) has monitored vaccine safety since 1990 — over a billion doses have been tracked with an exemplary safety record.
Aspirin, a drug available over the counter, causes more hospitalizations per year than all vaccines combined.
Phase III trials specifically enroll tens of thousands of people to detect even rare side effects before a vaccine reaches the public.
Every nation with a functioning health system, from Japan to Brazil to Germany, uses the same vaccines — if serious harms were common, this global consensus would have collapsed.
The mRNA COVID vaccines were authorized only after 40,000-person trials; the speed came from parallel manufacturing, not skipped steps.
